  "text_md": "10.00 10.40: Stefano Beggiora\n\n10.40 11.20: Davide Torri Panteion University of Social &amp; Political Sciences Department of Social Anthropology\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n## Programme 27th April\n\n9.30 10.00: Greetings and introduction to the workshop (Athina Athanasiou, Chair of Department of Social Anthropology; Eleana Yalouri; Director of the Laboratory for Anthropological Research For the Organizers: Diana Riboli, ISARS President, Lidia University of Cork) Guzy,\n\n## Session I\n\nChair: Lidia Guzy\n\nThe Khonds and the Jungle: A Case Study on Indigenous India\n\nSacred and Alive: Human, Non-human and Landscape in the (Buddhist) Himalayas\n\n11.20 11.40 Coffee Break\n\n11.40 - 12.20 Ivan Tacey\n\nRearranging Cosmic Relations: Cosmopolitics in the Anthropocene\n\n12.20-13.20 Discussion\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n13.30 - 14. 30 Lunch Break Session II Chair: Naran Bilik\n\n14.30 15.10 Taj Khan Kalash\n\nEcological Living in Peril: The Case of Kalasha Society in Hindu Kush\n\n15.10 15.50 Lu Fangfang\n\n15.50 16.30 Ranju Hasini Sahoo\n\nThe Making of Shaman among the Three Northern Minorities in China and the Hero's Theme\n\nAmarkantak: The Eco Cosmology and Sacred Complex\n\n16.30 17.30 Discussion\n\n## 28th April\n\nSession I Chair: Stefano Beggiora\n\n10.00- 10.40: Naran Bilik\n\nUnblocking the Blockage between Earth and Heaven: Shamanism as Cultural Intimacy in China\n\n<!-- image -->",
